# Ford Consul Classic four-door saloon, 1961-1963.
#
# The 109E/116E Consul Classic: the four-door with the quad headlamps in a
# wide chrome grille, the reverse-rake rear screen and the projecting roof
# overhang. 111,225 built across both body styles. It is NOT a Cortina and
# NOT the 1972-76 Granada-based Consul.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Consul_Classic
#
# Dimensions 4.337 x 1.651 x 1.422 m, wheelbase 2.515 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side elevation exists. Image 1 is about 40
# degrees off square; the flank is estimated from it and the front and rear
# three-quarters within the published dimensions. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (c), the Consul Capri 335 identification sheet's Ford plate
# codes and promotional names. Ermine White, Ambassador Blue, Goodwood Green
# and Monaco Red. Weights 8, 7, 5, 5, total 25, provisional.
#
# Speed 135 km/h. Comfort 55/413, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 55. Classes 1,2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1961 intro, retires staggered 1978-1981.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-consul-classic.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-consul-classic.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-consul-classic/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side elevation; images 2 and 3 govern
# the four-door build, and the two-door in image 1 and its non-standard alloys
# were excluded. The rear glass and roof corners are too angular, and the boot
# trim is simplified. At 128 px the quad lamps, reverse-rake screen and roof
# overhang read as a Consul Classic.


obj=citycar
name=FordConsulClassic(ErmineWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=8
